@localheinz Thank you for reporting and @AliabbasMerchant for weighing in. It's true that this is because we look up templates by scanning local files, which fails in these scenarios:

- when currently on a git branch that doesn't have templates, e.g. `gh-pages` https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/225#issuecomment-574377158;
- when using the `--repo OWNER/REPO` flag https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/503#issuecomment-588221632;
- when the repo inherits templates from an organization.

I would still classify this as a bug since templates aren't being applied in the same manner as on github.com.

@mislav Got your perspective :+1:

So how do we solve this? By getting the files via an HTTP call?  
(And maybe cache them somewhere for future use? :thinking: )

There is now an API for fetching pull request templates:
```graphql
query {
  repository(owner: "cli", name: "cli") {
    pullRequestTemplates{body,filename}
  }
}
```
This feature is now unblocked. Here is where we detect issue template API support: https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/3a4d947603603f5dea742442d32bc131e9786d25/pkg/cmd/pr/shared/templates.go#L138-L138

We could take a similar approach to detect API support for pull request templates too.
